  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SSB Tax for Development &#x2013; Statistics, Macroeconomic Analysis and Digital Public Goods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Statistics Norway&apos;s statistics and model-oriented Tax for Development projects will be to contribute to more efficient tax systems through more and better data for analysis and decision making. The statistics projects will especially be geared at supporting the availability of necessary statistics, data and analysis tools which are necessary preconditions for such analysis to be carried out in the first place. Furthermore, the project aims to contributing to improving capacity both for researchers and public officials to be able to carry out research and policy analysis related to taxes. 

Collaboration with African Union and ASEAN regarding implementation of the digital public good NADABAS &#x2013; a system for national accounts, which can help enhance transparency and accountability in terms of the state of national accounts, including revenues generated by sector, for comparison over time and across countries. SSB is piloting Statbus, an open source administrative registry for companies, in some countries. 

Components:
-Institutional cooperation with Malawi
-Institutional cooperation with Namibia
-Institutional cooperation with Ghana
-Limited cooperation with Kenya and possibly other countries
-Digital public goods - National Accounts Database System (NADABAS) - including cooperation with AU
-Digital public goods - Statistical business register (Statbus)</narrative>
  </description>
